 turnout among discontented voters, or a polling error of historic size, would be needed to put Hilton within striking distance.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Gavin Newsom (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "California's open governor's race pits Democrat Xavier Becerra against Republican Steve Hilton in a state that leans about 12 points Democratic. Polling since summer has consistently shown Becerra ahead by double digits, with recent surveys ranging from a 10-point to a 22-point margin. All seven expert raters call the race Solid or Safe Democratic, and prediction markets give Becerra roughly a 95% chance.\n\nHilton has run an unconventional campaign built on cheeky ads and messaging about voter discontent, and he has slightly outraised Becerra, but the only scheduled debate in early October did little to change the race's shape. Becerra has leaned on his experience while offering few specifics on taxes. The fundamentals and polling both point to a comfortable Democratic hold on the governorship.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9963, "margin": 17.38}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9982, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9936, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9916, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9966, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9966, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9808, "margin": 14.8}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9828, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9795, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9678, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9677, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9665, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9753,